  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Pat'Enfoliz is an independent pet-sitting service launched in early 2025, covering the area from Toulon to Hyères exclusively at the owner's home: the website says the sitter's own home is not suited to host animals, so there is no boarding. Its founder holds a BEPA and a professional baccalaureate in dog and cat breeding management, trained as a dog trainer and worked as one for 5 years, then ran a pet shop for 7 years. He holds the ACACED certificate (renewed in November 2024), a canine and feline first-aid introduction, PECCRAM training (April 2025) and a category 1 and 2 dog-keeping permit obtained in 2013. The activity is declared and covered by professional liability insurance specific to animal trades.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>Home visits happen one to three times a day. Classic formula (30-minute visit, 20-minute walk): €15 for one visit a day, €29 for two, €43 for three. Premium formula (1-hour visit, 50-minute walk, treats and extras such as shutters, plants or mail): €21, €41 or €61 a day. Walks alone cost €13 (30 min), €17 (1 h) or €33 (2 h), with lower rates for up to 5 outings. Each visit includes bowl cleaning, basic care (food, water, medication, health check) and a text report with photos or videos. Food supplements and prescription tablets can be given after a discussion at the first meeting; injections and veterinary care stay with animal health professionals. Extras: +€8 a day for several animals, +€5 on Sundays and public holidays, a €10 flat fee (up to 10 km) then €0.60/km for a vet trip, +€1 a day if the dog is in training. Stays of 4 to 7 days get 5% off, 8 to 14 days 7% off.</p>
      <p>The first meeting, used to sign the contract, meet your dog and hand over the keys, is free with no time limit. For walks, the site announces individual outings or very small groups (2 to 3 compatible dogs at most), in your neighbourhood, in parks that allow dogs, or on nature walks if you wish. You provide the harness or collar and the leash; waste bags are supplied. Other walk prices: two 30-minute outings €25.50, a pack of ten 1-hour walks €155, monthly subscription at −12%. The site says the service can be reached by phone 7 days a week, and the contact form is open 24/7.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: as with any at-home pet sitting, plan a first meeting before leaving on holiday, so your dog and their sitter get to know each other beforehand.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The covered area includes ten communes: Toulon, Hyères, Le Pradet, Carqueiranne, La Garde, La Valette-du-Var, La Farlède, Le Revest, La Crau and Solliès. The site mentions optional walks in calm places such as the forest, the sea or the countryside; ask at the first meeting which ones are possible for your dog.</p>
